      ],
      "content": "TL 00 SW         NETTLEDEN WITH         NETTLEDEN                  POTTEN END             (North side) 3/213                                   Pipers Cottage - GV                                      II House. C16, C19 brick additions at NE. Timber frame cased in rendered brickwork, frame exposed on gables. Steep red tile roofs. A 1½ storeys house of 3 structural bays facing S with 3 large gabled dormers rising through the eaves and lower brick ranges at E end and rear. 4 windows long. 3-light flush casements with lattice leaded glazing. Large canted bays at E and W ends. Posts and rails partially exposed internally on ground floor with cross-beams and axial beams. Wall plate some 4ft above floor level and 3 trusses with heavy curved braces to tie-beams (now cut through). Weathered timbers on former E end of house. Mid-height rail in rear (N) wall some 6ft from ground and 4ft below wallplate.  (RCHM Typescript). Listing NGR: TL0201410452"
    }
  ],
